{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229500-mapping-colors-of-jade-to-autochthon-s-6-elements","id":1229500,"title":"Mapping colors of jade to Autochthon's 6 elements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-22T20:16:23-07:00","id":1229500,"title":"Mapping colors of jade to Autochthon's 6 elements","content":"So as some of you know I'm currently embroiled in an attempt to bring alchemicals into 3E using mostly the rules for artifacts and evocations. To further this, I've been focusing on which 2E alchemical charms fit with the paradigms of each magical material as laid out in Arms of the Chosen (with the addition of adamant of course).<br /> <br /> This presents something of a difficulty with jade. The more metaphorical expressions of jade are of course unaffected, but the elemental expressions are quite inappropriate for Autochthonia. Who would expect a champion to have <i>wood </i>growing out of them or to have evocations based on stone? So I came up with the following Autochthonian alternates to the elemental aspects of jade:<br /> <br /> First, since jade is the magical material associated with the element of metal I think that all five colors should be linked with metal in approximately equal strength. This leaves 5 elements to distribute.<br /> <br /> White = Crystal (fairly obvious link here. Crystals are often found underground and this is the element closest to earth/stone)<br /> Black = Oil (once again, strong links here with the liquid/fluid elements. The color even fits nicely for an association with crude oil, though most oil used as lubricant would be far lighter color)<br /> Red = smoke (where there's smoke there's fire. The elemental association is quite clear, though this is actually the greatest metaphorical difference of all of them I've gone with)<br /> Blue = Steam (I'm mostly linking the two based on clouds and such, though the element of steam is noted as often being the hottest of the elements while blue jade is often associated with cold and ice)<br /> Green = Lightning (this is based on three things and was sort of the odd one out but it kinda works. 1. a tree bears a superficial resemblance to a sheet of lightning 2. Wood and lightning share certain traits of wildness and inability to be restrained fully without careful tending and 3. green jade is associated with life and vitality and I think we all know what you hit an experiment with to give it life! Plus iirc Alchemicals themselves are catalyzed by a bolt of Autochthon's essence which may or may not be lightning in that context)<br /> <br /> So, this is the way that I would arrange them, but can anyone argue for switching them around some? Are there are arrangements that better fit the metaphysical attributes of the elements together? I'm certainly not completely happy with the pairings, but the colors of jade were never written with Autochthonian elements in mind so there's bound to be some compromises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T20:50:04-07:00","id":1229505,"title":"","content":"White seems a better match for Metal's stability.<br /> <br /> Red for Lightning's energy.<br /> <br /> Blue for Crystal, given that ice is crystalline and Crystal is Autocthon's brain.<br /> <br /> Green for Steam, since it's the &quot;life-giving&quot; element?<br /> <br /> Black for Oil works well.<br /> <br /> Nothing for Smoke, which is the element of death and decay representing the Great Maker's mortality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T20:53:16-07:00","id":1229506,"title":"","content":"I think I would do something more like:<br /> Crystal = Green (growth and such)<br /> Lightning = Blue (cognition, also Air is already associated with lightning etc)<br /> Metal = White (Ore, and metal is to Autochthon as stone is to Creation)<br /> Steam = Red (impetus, heat)<br /> Oil = Black (fluidity, flexibilty)<br /> <br /> That leaves smoke, which is more a product of Autothon's illness. Maps to Soulsteel, the least natural of the 5MM as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T21:13:50-07:00","id":1229507,"title":"","content":"&quot;Crystal&quot; themed evocations would probably also overlap heavily with Adamant Artifact evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T21:32:36-07:00","id":1229510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229500-mapping-colors-of-jade-to-autochthon-s-6-elements?p=1229505#post1229505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White seems a better match for Metal's stability.<br /> <br /> Red for Lightning's energy.<br /> <br /> Blue for Crystal, given that ice is crystalline and Crystal is Autocthon's brain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, metal is crystalline. Also, a lot of associations with Earth and Metal got stripped out in WFHW, so the connection between those two isn't quite so strong. And if we're talking about stability, that might go over better with Crystal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Green for Steam, since it's the &quot;life-giving&quot; element? </div> </div> </div>Steam, being water and fire together, would be more likely to be Black and Red together. Perhaps we can call it fused jade. As for Wood, it's related to concepts that Autochthonia doesn't really have much truck with, like growing out of the ground when the sun shines just right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Black for Oil works well.<br /> <br /> Nothing for Smoke, which is the element of death and decay representing the Great Maker's mortality. </div> </div> </div>But Smoke is Air. Bad air, to be sure, but air nonetheless. So you might get stained versions of blue jade in Autochthonia, and have to clean those items frequently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T21:54:04-07:00","id":1229512,"title":"","content":"The ones that fit well are...<br /> <br /> Black: fluidity themed evocations (Oil)<br /> Blue: cognition and lightning themed evocations (Lightning)<br /> Red: heat &amp; pressure themed evocations (Steam)<br /> White: stability, strength, and magnetism themed evocations (Metal)<br /> <br /> As most &quot;crystaline&quot; themed evocations will come from Adamant Artifacts, and most death &amp; refuse themed evocations will come from Soulsteel Artifacts - that leaves Green Jade kind of the weird one out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T22:24:12-07:00","id":1229516,"title":"","content":"5 types of jade with 6 elements does get messy quick with either double representations or odd man out scenarios.<br /> <br /> Doing a combo method of two jade types per element gives ten options for six elements:<br /> Steam= fire &amp; water=black &amp; red<br /> Metal= fire &amp; earth= white &amp; red<br /> Lightning= air &amp; (fire or wood)= blue &amp; red/green<br /> Oil= water &amp; (earth or wood)= black &amp; white/green<br /> Smoke= air &amp; (earth or fire or wood)= blue &amp; white/red/green<br /> Crystal= earth &amp; wood= white &amp; green<br /> <br /> How do you want certain elements symbolized? Is smoke based on things burning, or what was burned or the particulates now in the air. Oil has stuff in it, so it becomes flammable or fire based or is an organic substance and so more woodlike?<br /> <br /> Answering that stuff may help answer those questions. Checking all of the associations between classic exalts and alchemicals might help as well. Or may confuse it worse to be honest.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of work went into making alchemicals not fit the 5 points of Creation on purpose though, so either bump out an element or add a jade (yellow may be needed for this experiment) if matches must be made","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T05:14:25-07:00","id":1229566,"title":"","content":"MoeP: Alchemicals does provide a rough canonical correspondence between creation and autochthonian elements in the form of the charm Industrial Survival Frame, which is split into the six autochthonian elements but also provides protection against creation-based hazards.<br /> <br /> Crystal protects against &quot;natural&quot; stuff, like cave ins and thorny plants, so kind of a hybrid of earth and wood. (It also provides more general protection in the form of mimicking integrity-protecting prana because those things are like rocking horse shit in autochthonia and it needed some utility there, but that's not really relevant here.)<br /> <br /> Lightning protects against fire and lightning. So Fire/air there.<br /> <br /> Metal is just, well, metal. So the rest of earth I guess?<br /> <br /> Oil protects against acid and other chemicals, so uh, vitriol I guess. But Water would fit too. <br /> <br /> Smoke protects against poison so there's some more of wood.<br /> <br /> Steam protects against temperature extremes and pressure. So there's some fire, air <i>and</i> water there.<br /> <br /> So, it seems a bit like they're all spread out over a bunch of things. I dunno if this helped at all but I figure it's worth noting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T07:37:41-07:00","id":1229596,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar456_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"456\" data-vbnamecard=\"456\">Blackwell</a> Except that smoke is literally one of the things that red jade is already associated with. It's on red jades list! On the other hand Autochthon's smoke is associated with soulsteel so you're not wrong<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> Yes... and? Moonsilver = oil, soulsteel = smoke etc. I guess it would help if I mentioned that this exercise is at least partially based on trying to create an Industrial Survival Frame equivalent, but being forced to make it out of a single magical material for resonance purposes? Jade seemed the obvious choice for that. Because elements<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cryo-Seraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229500-mapping-colors-of-jade-to-autochthon-s-6-elements?p=1229516#post1229516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 types of jade with 6 elements does get messy quick with either double representations or odd man out scenarios.<br /> <br /> Doing a combo method of two jade types per element gives ten options for six elements:<br /> Steam= fire &amp; water=black &amp; red<br /> Metal= fire &amp; earth= white &amp; red<br /> Lightning= air &amp; (fire or wood)= blue &amp; red/green<br /> Oil= water &amp; (earth or wood)= black &amp; white/green<br /> Smoke= air &amp; (earth or fire or wood)= blue &amp; white/red/green<br /> Crystal= earth &amp; wood= white &amp; green</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course with this layout, either green and white are emphasized, being linked to more elements than the others or red jade is seemingly linked to everything. Unavoidable<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cryo-Seraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229500-mapping-colors-of-jade-to-autochthon-s-6-elements?p=1229516#post1229516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you want certain elements symbolized? Is smoke based on things burning, or what was burned or the particulates now in the air. Oil has stuff in it, so it becomes flammable or fire based or is an organic substance and so more woodlike?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any of these could work. I'm basically just looking for the strongest links without matching something completely weird like crystal=black jade or something. I went with green=sheets of lightning and vitality so I'm not opposed to a somewhat looser link. If someone can present a better mapping of links then I'll go with that.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cryo-Seraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229500-mapping-colors-of-jade-to-autochthon-s-6-elements?p=1229516#post1229516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Answering that stuff may help answer those questions. Checking all of the associations between classic exalts and alchemicals might help as well. Or may confuse it worse to be honest.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of work went into making alchemicals not fit the 5 points of Creation on purpose though, so either bump out an element or add a jade (yellow may be needed for this experiment) if matches must be made</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh absolutely, Like I said they don't map perfectly to creation's elements. However, the magical materials DO match up to Autochthon's elements and jade = metal. Not white jade or red jade or black jade but <i>jade</i>.<br /> <br /> Hence why in my odd man out scenario I chose metal to be the odd man out and linked to all 5 types of jade.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> and if I could actually port that charm as is it would be so much easier, but treating it as an artifact forces me to choose one MM that determines who resonates with it.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... I suppose I could ditch the attempt entirely and just go with each MM expresses their associated element directly and jade is just metal. The 'artifact would still be jade resonant as it would be the biggest portion of the charm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T08:24:34-07:00","id":1229601,"title":"","content":"...Maybe you could just have autochthonian jade be six completely different colours and associate with the elements directly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T10:44:03-07:00","id":1229615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229500-mapping-colors-of-jade-to-autochthon-s-6-elements?p=1229566#post1229566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MoeP: Alchemicals does provide a rough canonical correspondence between creation and autochthonian elements in the form of the charm Industrial Survival Frame, which is split into the six autochthonian elements but also provides protection against creation-based hazards.<br /> <br /> Crystal protects against &quot;natural&quot; stuff, like cave ins and thorny plants, so kind of a hybrid of earth and wood. (It also provides more general protection in the form of mimicking integrity-protecting prana because those things are like rocking horse shit in autochthonia and it needed some utility there, but that's not really relevant here.)<br /> <br /> Lightning protects against fire and lightning. So Fire/air there.<br /> <br /> <b>Metal is just, well, metal. So the rest of earth I guess?</b><br /> <br /> Oil protects against acid and other chemicals, so uh, vitriol I guess. But Water would fit too.<br /> <br /> Smoke protects against poison so there's some more of wood.<br /> <br /> Steam protects against temperature extremes and pressure. So there's some fire, air <i>and</i> water there.<br /> <br /> So, it seems a bit like they're all spread out over a bunch of things. I dunno if this helped at all but I figure it's worth noting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Metal is explicitly not something that the Dragon-Blooded elemental protection Charm for Earth protects against in WFHW, though. Fire, I believe, is what you need to defend against metal weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T10:51:10-07:00","id":1229616,"title":"","content":"So thinking about it, I realized that I was thinking too much like someone from our word or Creation when i was resistant to associating Green Jade with Smoke. Autochthonia doesn\u2019t have plant life for people to associate \u201cgreen\u201d with natural vibrancy the way we do. Toxic clouds would be among the most natural associations for the color for them, and appropriately enough its green jade that poison-based Evocations typically come from.<br /> <br /> So<br /> <br /> Blue - Lightning<br /> Black - Oil<br /> Green - Smoke<br /> Red - Steam<br /> White - Metal<br /> <br /> Which leaves Crystal the odd element out. But that strikes me as thematically appropriate as it\u2019s the element associated with divinity, the secret Caste of Alchemicals, etc. if you need some crystal-themed effect from Jade, have it require all the colors ala a prism!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-23-2018, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T15:11:39-07:00","id":1229661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229500-mapping-colors-of-jade-to-autochthon-s-6-elements?p=1229616#post1229616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So thinking about it, I realized that I was thinking too much like someone from our word or Creation when i was resistant to associating Green Jade with Smoke. Autochthonia doesn\u2019t have plant life for people to associate \u201cgreen\u201d with natural vibrancy the way we do. Toxic clouds would be among the most natural associations for the color for them, and appropriately enough its green jade that poison-based Evocations typically come from.<br /> <br /> So<br /> <br /> Blue - Lightning<br /> Black - Oil<br /> Green - Smoke<br /> Red - Steam<br /> White - Metal<br /> <br /> Which leaves Crystal the odd element out. But that strikes me as thematically appropriate as it\u2019s the element associated with divinity, the secret Caste of Alchemicals, etc. if you need some crystal-themed effect from Jade, have it require all the colors ala a prism!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... mostly I like this actually, though I'd switch out crystal and metal.<br /> <br /> As I've said, metal fits with jade in general as per the main MM links. And it's not like crystal doesn't fit with white jade at all.<br /> <br /> Also, I've been thinking of the different ways that all five fit with metal and here goes:<br /> <br /> white - magnetism and solidity<br /> Black - Mercury and liquid metals in general in Autochthon's body<br /> red - Superheated metal, how conductive metal is, hell metal even turns a nice cherry red at high temperatures (though of course it goes more yellow and then white at higher still), and metals like magnesium<br /> Green - here I'm thinking more along the lines of metallic poisons such as arsenic or basically any heavy metal poisoning<br /> Blue - This one is the hardest to link I think. Open to suggestions here as well of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T15:22:31-07:00","id":1229664,"title":"","content":"Another way to think about this is where you might find different jades incorporated into Autochthon's body<br /> <br /> Green jade - smoke filters, repair subsystems perhaps? Nutrient slurry veins?<br /> Black jade - Fluid management, adaptive systems (immune system?), lubricated joints or bearings<br /> Red - Steam channels, slag tubes, heating coils<br /> Blue Jade - Coolant systems, duct work, lightning generators (tesla coils perhaps?)<br /> Whit jade - structural points, wear-resistant surfaces, Magnetic fields","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T19:47:49-07:00","id":1229711,"title":"","content":"If you want to associate Jade with Metal specifically in Autochthonian Evocation/Charm tech, the other elements have magical material associations provided by the Alchemicals Castes too.<br /> <br /> Crystal - Adamant<br /> Lightning - Orichalcum<br /> Oil - Moonsilver<br /> Smoke - Soulsteel<br /> Steam - Starmetal<br /> <br /> Obviously the Steam/Starmetal association is the weakest, but it\u2019s necessary to make the rest of the pattern work (1st Edition associated the Starmetal Caste with Crystal, but the canonization of the Adamant Caste made changing that necessary).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T21:19:21-07:00","id":1229735,"title":"","content":"Must admit that considering lack of discussion of jade colors in Autochthonia, that is both a world and the body of a living Primordial, i would be kind of tempted to just go with something in the vein of Underworld's pervasiveness of a white jade with qualities somewhat peculiar to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T23:06:07-07:00","id":1229749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229500-mapping-colors-of-jade-to-autochthon-s-6-elements?p=1229711#post1229711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to associate Jade with Metal specifically in Autochthonian Evocation/Charm tech, the other elements have magical material associations provided by the Alchemicals Castes too.<br /> <br /> Crystal - Adamant<br /> Lightning - Orichalcum<br /> Oil - Moonsilver<br /> Smoke - Soulsteel<br /> Steam - Starmetal<br /> <br /> Obviously the Steam/Starmetal association is the weakest, but it\u2019s necessary to make the rest of the pattern work (1st Edition associated the Starmetal Caste with Crystal, but the canonization of the Adamant Caste made changing that necessary).</div> </div> </div> </div>You know that this was how it was set up in 2E right? This is exactly the associations made in the caste descriptions.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I agree that it is possible to go with each MM being directly linked to an element and leave it at that, but I can't help but think about how jade is supposed to be the MM that has the raw expressions of elemental energy. I kinda want to preserve that at least somewhat.<br /> <br /> Plus as I said upthread it's easier to say that the Industrial Survival Frame is a jade artifact than an artifact made out of all 6 MM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T23:23:14-07:00","id":1229750,"title":"","content":"I... know that, that\u2019s why i said the associations were provided by the Alchemical Castes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T06:03:03-07:00","id":1229789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229500-mapping-colors-of-jade-to-autochthon-s-6-elements?p=1229750#post1229750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... know that, that\u2019s why i said the associations were provided by the Alchemical Castes.</div> </div> </div> </div>okay, it's just that you were listing them off like <i>I </i>didn't know that when I had already responded to you pointing out that crystal =adamant in my second post in the thread. It seemed like you had missed that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}